<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <title>{assigns[:page_title] || @window.label}</title>
    <%!--
      The machine-readable window spec. A native shell scrapes this on load and
      configures the native window; the LiveView stays authoritative about WHAT
      the window is, the shell about HOW to realise it. See PQCompanion.Shell.
    --%>
    <meta name="pq-window" content={Jason.encode!(PQCompanion.Windows.meta_payload(@window))} />
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/js/app.js"}></script>
  </head>
  <%!-- body-transparent is what makes the window see-through; the reference
       achieved this by mutating document.body.style in a React effect, which is
       what produced the "overlay turned into a black box" bug when a render
       threw. A class on the shell cannot be left in the wrong state. --%>
  <body class="body-transparent bg-transparent">
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
